{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nYou are given set of n points in 5-dimensional space. The points are labeled from 1 to n. No two points coincide.We will call point a bad if there are different points b and c, not equal to a, from the given set such that angle between vectors  and  is acute (i.e. strictly less than ). Otherwise, the point is called good.The angle between vectors  and  in 5-dimensional space is defined as , where  is the scalar product and  is length of .Given the list of points, print the indices of the good points in ascending order.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        FastReader fr = new FastReader();\n        int n = fr.nextInt();\n        if (n > 10) {\n            System.out.println(0);\n            return;\n        }\n        int[][] pts = new int[n][5];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < 5; j++) {\n                pts[i][j] = fr.nextInt();\n            }\n        }\n        List<Integer> good = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            boolean ok = true;\n            for (int j = 0; j < n && ok; j++) {\n                if (i == j) continue;\n                for (int k = j + 1; k < n && ok; k++) {\n                    if (i == k) continue;\n                    if (angle(pts[i], pts[j], pts[k]) < 90) {\n                        ok = false;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            if (ok) good.add(i + 1);\n        }\n        System.out.println(good.size());\n        good.forEach(System.out::println);\n    }\n\n    static double angle(int[] o, int[] a, int[] b) {\n        double dot = 0, la = 0, lb = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < o.length; i++) {\n            double x = a[i] - o[i];\n            double y = b[i] - o[i];\n            dot += x * y;\n            la += x * x;\n            lb += y * y;\n        }\n        return Math.toDegrees(Math.acos(dot / Math.sqrt(la * lb)));\n    }\n\n    static class FastReader {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public FastReader() {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n\n        String next() throws Exception {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() throws Exception {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        FastReader fr = new FastReader();\n        int n = fr.nextInt();\n        int[][] pts = new int[n][5];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < 5; j++) {\n                pts[i][j] = fr.nextInt();\n            }\n        }\n        List<Integer> good = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            boolean isGood = true;\n            // Check all pairs of distinct points b and c (b != c, b != i, c != i)\n            for (int b = 0; b < n && isGood; b++) {\n                if (b == i) continue;\n                for (int c = b + 1; c < n && isGood; c++) {\n                    if (c == i) continue;\n                    // Check if angle between vectors (i->b) and (i->c) is acute\n                    if (isAcuteAngle(pts[i], pts[b], pts[c])) {\n                        isGood = false;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            if (isGood) {\n                good.add(i + 1);\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(good.size());\n        for (int idx : good) {\n            System.out.println(idx);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Check if angle between vectors OA and OB is acute\n    // Vectors are from point O to points A and B respectively\n    static boolean isAcuteAngle(int[] o, int[] a, int[] b) {\n        long dot = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n            long x = (long)a[i] - o[i];\n            long y = (long)b[i] - o[i];\n            dot += x * y;\n        }\n        // If dot product > 0, angle is acute (less than 90 degrees)\n        return dot > 0;\n    }\n\n    static class FastReader {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public FastReader() {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n\n        String next() throws Exception {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() throws Exception {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n<